{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00352 - MONDO_17894",
  "verbalization": "Tioguanine appears to be linked to Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a shared pathway involving Idarubicin, a chemotherapy agent. The evidence suggests that Tioguanine is indicated for various forms of myeloid leukemia, including Inherited AML and Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, all of which are associated with Idarubicin. Idarubicin, in turn, is linked to AML with Cebpa somatic mutations, indicating a potential mechanism by which Tioguanine may influence the development or progression of this disease. The overlapping indications and the presence of a common downstream target (Idarubicin) suggest a possible role for Tioguanine in the treatment or pathogenesis of AML with Cebpa mutations. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential link between Tioguanine and AML, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
